WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.200
Where would you like to

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.770
keep your Continuum memory?

3
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.120
Continuum creates a folder for

4
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.480
its working copy of your

5
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.720
conversations and the personal guide

6
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.160
it builds from them.

7
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.440
You can keep that folder

8
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:14.720
on this Mac or on

9
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:22.080
an external drive.

10
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.440
Keeping it on the Mac

11
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.720
is usually simpler.

12
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.160
Your history is available when

13
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.840
you're using the computer, without

14
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:35.360
connecting another device.

15
00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.920
An external drive saves space

16
00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:38.960
on the Mac.

17
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.480
The trade-off is that you'll

18
00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:41.440
need to plug it in

19
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.200
whenever Continuum needs to look

20
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.880
up a conversation or save

21
00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:46.080
an update.

22
00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.760
If the drive is missing,

23
00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:49.200
the assistant should tell you

24
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.440
it can't reach that history.

25
00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.280
The estimate below shows how

26
00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.600
much space your selected files

27
00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.110
may need.

28
00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:58.790
Leave some extra room:

29
00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:01.270
adding more conversations or another

30
00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:02.630
way to search them will

31
00:01:02.630 --> 00:01:04.390
make the folder grow.

32
00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:06.070
Choose a folder that stays

33
00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:07.910
on your computer or drive,

34
00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:10.150
rather than one automatically copied

35
00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.390
to a cloud storage service.

36
00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:14.150
The setup assistant will check

37
00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:22.230
the location before continuing.

38
00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.150
The Continuum program stays on

39
00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.750
your Mac either way.

40
00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:27.510
This choice only decides where

41
00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:29.350
its working memory lives.

42
00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:37.510
Your original downloads stay unchanged.

43
00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:38.630
Would you like to use

44
00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:40.150
this Mac or an external

45
00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:41.230
drive?
